IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-interpretation`
IMPORT `g6-art15-16-deregistration`
IMPORT `g6-art17-after-deregistration`

-- g6-tests-art17.l4: tests of Article 17 (Effects of deregistration).
-- Every expected value was decided from the text of the Law before the module was first run; the quotation above a group is the text it comes from.
-- A DEONTIC cannot be compared in #ASSERT, so duties, powers and prohibitions are exercised by #TRACE, each with its outcome in the `-- EXPECT:` comment above it
-- (read by work/g6/check-traces.py); the facts behind them are asserted on the BOOLEAN and DATE rules. Retention is exercised on the date-serial clock (AT (Day (YMD ...))).

§ `Tests of Article 17`

§§ `Fixtures`

`the route of a deregistration for misleading` MEANS `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity`
`the route of a deregistration because the entity no longer exists` MEANS `by written notice under Article 16(2) because the entity no longer exists`
`the route of a deregistration on application` MEANS `on the entity's own application under Article 15(3)(a)`

-- Positional construction of a deregistration: the route; the date of the deregistration; the date of the preliminary notice; the date the Commissioner is satisfied the grounds have existed since;
-- the past date specified in the deregistration notice; the past date specified in the preliminary notice; the Commissioner determines the deregistration takes effect retrospectively.
-- The survey's case for F6.3: preliminary notice 1 March 2026, deregistration notice 1 April 2026, past date 1 January 2025 specified in the deregistration notice.
`a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice` MEANS `Deregistration of the entity` OF `the route of a deregistration for misleading`, (YMD 2026 4 1), (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)), (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), NOTHING, TRUE
`a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the preliminary notice only` MEANS `Deregistration of the entity` OF `the route of a deregistration for misleading`, (YMD 2026 4 1), (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)), (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), NOTHING, (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), TRUE
`a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in both notices` MEANS `Deregistration of the entity` OF `the route of a deregistration for misleading`, (YMD 2026 4 1), (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)), (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), TRUE
`a deregistration under Article 16(2) with a past date` MEANS `Deregistration of the entity` OF `the route of a deregistration because the entity no longer exists`, (YMD 2026 4 1), NOTHING, (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), NOTHING, TRUE
`a deregistration on application with a past date` MEANS `Deregistration of the entity` OF `the route of a deregistration on application`, (YMD 2026 4 1), NOTHING, (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), NOTHING, TRUE
`a deregistration where the Commissioner does not determine retrospective effect` MEANS `Deregistration of the entity` OF `the route of a deregistration for misleading`, (YMD 2026 4 1), (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)), (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), NOTHING, FALSE
`a deregistration where the Commissioner is not satisfied of any past date` MEANS `Deregistration of the entity` OF `the route of a deregistration for misleading`, (YMD 2026 4 1), (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)), NOTHING, (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), NOTHING, TRUE
`a deregistration where the date specified is not the date the Commissioner is satisfied of` MEANS `Deregistration of the entity` OF `the route of a deregistration for misleading`, (YMD 2026 4 1), (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)), (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), (JUST (YMD 2025 2 1)), NOTHING, TRUE
`a deregistration where no date is specified in the notice` MEANS `Deregistration of the entity` OF `the route of a deregistration for misleading`, (YMD 2026 4 1), (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)), (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)), NOTHING, NOTHING, TRUE
`a deregistration where the past date is the day of the notice itself` MEANS `Deregistration of the entity` OF `the route of a deregistration for misleading`, (YMD 2026 4 1), (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)), (JUST (YMD 2026 4 1)), (JUST (YMD 2026 4 1)), NOTHING, TRUE
`a deregistration where the past date is after the day of the notice` MEANS `Deregistration of the entity` OF `the route of a deregistration for misleading`, (YMD 2026 4 1), (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)), (JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)), (JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)), NOTHING, TRUE
`a deregistration without retrospective effect` MEANS `Deregistration of the entity` OF `the route of a deregistration for misleading`, (YMD 2026 4 1), (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)), NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE

§§ `Article 17(2) and (3) -- retrospective effect`

-- src:446 | (2) Paragraph (3) applies if the Commissioner –
-- src:447 | (a) deregisters a charity under Article 16;
-- src:448 | (b) is satisfied that the grounds for deregistration have existed since a past date;
-- src:449 | (c) specifies that date in the notice under Article 16(1) or (2); and
-- src:450 | (d) determines that the deregistration should take effect retrospectively.
-- src:451 | (3) The termination takes effect from the past date specified under paragraph (2)(c) for all purposes, including the purposes of any enactment relating to taxation, but subject to paragraph (4).
-- (2) Paragraph (3) applies if the Commissioner (a) deregisters a charity under Article 16; (b) is satisfied that the grounds have existed since a past date; (c) specifies that date in the notice; and (d) determines retrospective effect.
#ASSERT       `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice`
#ASSERT       `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in both notices`
-- (a): under Article 15 there is no retrospective effect, whatever else is true; under Article 16(2) there may be.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `the readings taken` `a deregistration on application with a past date`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(2)(a) the Commissioner deregisters a charity under Article 16` `a deregistration on application with a past date`
#ASSERT       `Art 17(2)(a) the Commissioner deregisters a charity under Article 16` `a deregistration under Article 16(2) with a past date`
#ASSERT       `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `the readings taken` `a deregistration under Article 16(2) with a past date`
-- (b), (c), (d): each is needed.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `the readings taken` `a deregistration where the Commissioner is not satisfied of any past date`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `the readings taken` `a deregistration where the date specified is not the date the Commissioner is satisfied of`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `the readings taken` `a deregistration where no date is specified in the notice`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `the readings taken` `a deregistration where the Commissioner does not determine retrospective effect`
-- "A past date" is a date before the date of the notice: the day of the notice itself, or a later day, is not a past date.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `the readings taken` `a deregistration where the past date is the day of the notice itself`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `the readings taken` `a deregistration where the past date is after the day of the notice`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `the readings taken` `a deregistration without retrospective effect`
-- Limbs (b) and (c) on their own. The Commissioner is not satisfied of any past date: (b) fails, and so does (c), although a date is specified in the notice.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(2)(b) the Commissioner is satisfied that the grounds have existed since a past date` `the readings taken` `a deregistration where the Commissioner is not satisfied of any past date`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(2)(c) the Commissioner specifies that date in the notice` `the readings taken` `a deregistration where the Commissioner is not satisfied of any past date`
#ASSERT       `Art 17(2)(b) the Commissioner is satisfied that the grounds have existed since a past date` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice`
#ASSERT       `Art 17(2)(c) the Commissioner specifies that date in the notice` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(2)(c) the Commissioner specifies that date in the notice` `the readings taken` `a deregistration where no date is specified in the notice`
-- F6.3. The past date is specified in the preliminary notice only: not retrospective if "the notice" is the one by which the Commissioner deregisters; retrospective if it is the preliminary notice.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the preliminary notice only`
#ASSERT       `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` (`the readings taken but with F6.3 read as` `the preliminary notice that gives reasons and invites objections`) `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the preliminary notice only`
-- ... and the converse: specified in the deregistration notice only, it is retrospective on the first reading and not on the second.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` (`the readings taken but with F6.3 read as` `the preliminary notice that gives reasons and invites objections`) `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice`
-- Under Article 16(2) there is no preliminary notice: the one notice is the notice on both readings.
#ASSERT       `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` (`the readings taken but with F6.3 read as` `the preliminary notice that gives reasons and invites objections`) `a deregistration under Article 16(2) with a past date`

-- src:451 | (3) The termination takes effect from the past date specified under paragraph (2)(c) for all purposes, including the purposes of any enactment relating to taxation, but subject to paragraph (4).
-- (3) The termination takes effect from the past date specified, for all purposes, including the purposes of any enactment relating to taxation, but subject to paragraph (4).
#ASSERT       `Art 17(3) the date from which the termination takes effect` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)
#ASSERT       `Art 17(3) the date from which the termination takes effect` `the readings taken` `a deregistration without retrospective effect` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT       `Art 17(3) the date from which the termination takes effect` `the readings taken` `a deregistration on application with a past date` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The date the entity is treated as deregistered: the past date if retrospective, otherwise the date of the deregistration itself (IP7 `date deregistered`).
#ASSERT       `Art 17(3) the date deregistered` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice` EQUALS YMD 2025 1 1
#ASSERT       `Art 17(3) the date deregistered` `the readings taken` `a deregistration without retrospective effect` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 1
#ASSERT       `Art 17(3) the date deregistered` `the readings taken` `a deregistration on application with a past date` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 1

§§ `Article 17(4) -- an act before the notice is not made an offence by the retrospective effect`

-- src:452 | (4) An act, that occurred before the date of the giving of the notice under Article 16(1) or (2) is not rendered an offence merely by virtue of the operation of paragraph (3).
-- (4) An act that occurred before the date of the giving of the notice is not rendered an offence merely by virtue of the operation of paragraph (3).
-- Notice by which the Commissioner deregisters: 1 April 2026. An act on 15 March, 31 March: before it, so protected. An act on 1 April: not before it, so not protected. After: not protected.
#ASSERT       `Art 17(4) the act is not rendered an offence by the retrospective effect` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in both notices` (YMD 2026 3 15)
#ASSERT       `Art 17(4) the act is not rendered an offence by the retrospective effect` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in both notices` (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(4) the act is not rendered an offence by the retrospective effect` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in both notices` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(4) the act is not rendered an offence by the retrospective effect` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in both notices` (YMD 2026 4 2)
-- F6.3, the discriminating case: preliminary notice 1 March 2026, deregistration notice 1 April 2026, past date 1 January 2025; an act on 15 March 2026 (between the two notices, after the past date).
-- Protected if "the notice" is the one by which the Commissioner deregisters; not protected if it is the preliminary notice.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(4) the act is not rendered an offence by the retrospective effect` (`the readings taken but with F6.3 read as` `the preliminary notice that gives reasons and invites objections`) `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in both notices` (YMD 2026 3 15)
#ASSERT       `Art 17(4) the act is not rendered an offence by the retrospective effect` (`the readings taken but with F6.3 read as` `the preliminary notice that gives reasons and invites objections`) `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in both notices` (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(4) the act is not rendered an offence by the retrospective effect` (`the readings taken but with F6.3 read as` `the preliminary notice that gives reasons and invites objections`) `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in both notices` (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- Without retrospective effect there is nothing for paragraph (4) to save an act from.
#ASSERT       `Art 17(4) the act is not rendered an offence by the retrospective effect` `the readings taken` `a deregistration without retrospective effect` (YMD 2026 5 1)

§§ `Article 17(1) -- what the Commissioner does after deregistering`

-- Positional construction of the deregistration used for retention: the survey's case for F6.5, notice 1 June 2026, effective date 1 June 2021, asked on 1 January 2033.
`a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` MEANS `Deregistration of the entity` OF `the route of a deregistration for misleading`, (YMD 2026 6 1), NOTHING, (JUST (YMD 2021 6 1)), (JUST (YMD 2021 6 1)), NOTHING, TRUE
`a deregistration on 29 February 2028 without retrospective effect` MEANS `Deregistration of the entity` OF `the route of a deregistration on application`, (YMD 2028 2 29), NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE

-- src:443 | (1) After deregistering an entity, the Commissioner –
-- src:444 | (a) must retain the information registered in respect of that entity for 10 years; and
-- (a) must retain the information registered in respect of that entity for 10 years. From the notice (the reading taken) of 1 June 2026: the last day is 1 June 2036, and it may be discarded from 2 June 2036.
#ASSERT       `Art 17(1)(a) the last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` EQUALS YMD 2036 6 1
#ASSERT       `Art 17(1)(a) the Commissioner may discard the information on` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` EQUALS YMD 2036 6 2
-- F6.5: from the date from which the termination takes effect, 1 June 2021: the last day is 1 June 2031. Asked on 1 January 2033 the information may be discarded on the second reading, not on the first.
#ASSERT       `Art 17(1)(a) the last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` (`the readings taken but with F6.5 read as` `the ten years run from the date from which the termination takes effect`) `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` EQUALS YMD 2031 6 1
#ASSERT NOT   (YMD 2033 1 1) AT LEAST `Art 17(1)(a) the Commissioner may discard the information on` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021`
#ASSERT       (YMD 2033 1 1) AT LEAST `Art 17(1)(a) the Commissioner may discard the information on` (`the readings taken but with F6.5 read as` `the ten years run from the date from which the termination takes effect`) `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021`
-- F6.18, counting: the day before the anniversary, 31 May 2036.
#ASSERT       `Art 17(1)(a) the last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` (`the readings taken but with F6.18 read as` `the last day is the day before the anniversary`) `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` EQUALS YMD 2036 5 31
-- Started on 29 February 2028 (no retrospective effect): 28 February 2038 on the reading taken, 1 March 2038 where 29 February rolls, 27 February 2038 on the day-before reading.
#ASSERT       `Art 17(1)(a) the last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` `the readings taken` `a deregistration on 29 February 2028 without retrospective effect` EQUALS YMD 2038 2 28
#ASSERT       `Art 17(1)(a) the last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` (`the readings taken but with F6.18 read as` `the last day is the anniversary, and 29 February rolls to 1 March`) `a deregistration on 29 February 2028 without retrospective effect` EQUALS YMD 2038 3 1
#ASSERT       `Art 17(1)(a) the last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` (`the readings taken but with F6.18 read as` `the last day is the day before the anniversary`) `a deregistration on 29 February 2028 without retrospective effect` EQUALS YMD 2038 2 27
-- The length of the ten years from 1 June 2026, in days: 3,653 (three leap days, 29 February 2028, 2032 and 2036, fall inside).
#ASSERT       `the number of days from the start of the ten years to their last day` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` EQUALS 3653

-- The duty, on the date-serial clock: starting on the day the ten years start (1 June 2026), discarding on the last day (1 June 2036) is the failure; discarding on 2 June 2036 is not.
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 17(1)(a)
#TRACE `Art 17(1)(a) the Commissioner must retain the information for 10 years` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` AT (Day (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard the information registered in respect of the entity` `the Commissioner` AT (Day (YMD 2036 6 1))
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(1)(a) the Commissioner must retain the information for 10 years` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` AT (Day (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard the information registered in respect of the entity` `the Commissioner` AT (Day (YMD 2036 6 2))
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 17(1)(a)
#TRACE `Art 17(1)(a) the Commissioner must retain the information for 10 years` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` AT (Day (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard the information registered in respect of the entity` `the Commissioner` AT (Day (YMD 2027 1 1))
-- Nothing discarded: the prohibition stands until its last day has passed.
-- EXPECT: STANDING discard the information registered in respect of the entity
#TRACE `Art 17(1)(a) the Commissioner must retain the information for 10 years` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` AT (Day (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` (Day (YMD 2030 1 1)))
-- F6.5: counted from 1 June 2021 the last day is 1 June 2031, so discarding on 1 January 2033 is free.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(1)(a) the Commissioner must retain the information for 10 years` (`the readings taken but with F6.5 read as` `the ten years run from the date from which the termination takes effect`) `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` AT (Day (YMD 2021 6 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard the information registered in respect of the entity` `the Commissioner` AT (Day (YMD 2033 1 1))
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 17(1)(a)
#TRACE `Art 17(1)(a) the Commissioner must retain the information for 10 years` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` AT (Day (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard the information registered in respect of the entity` `the Commissioner` AT (Day (YMD 2033 1 1))
-- F6.18, the day before the anniversary: discarding on 1 June 2036 is free, on 31 May 2036 it is not.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(1)(a) the Commissioner must retain the information for 10 years` (`the readings taken but with F6.18 read as` `the last day is the day before the anniversary`) `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` AT (Day (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard the information registered in respect of the entity` `the Commissioner` AT (Day (YMD 2036 6 1))
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 17(1)(a)
#TRACE `Art 17(1)(a) the Commissioner must retain the information for 10 years` (`the readings taken but with F6.18 read as` `the last day is the day before the anniversary`) `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` AT (Day (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard the information registered in respect of the entity` `the Commissioner` AT (Day (YMD 2036 5 31))

-- src:445 | (b) must not assign the registered number of that entity to any other registered charity.
-- (b) must not assign the registered number of that entity to any other registered charity. No period is stated: on the reading taken the bar has no end, so assigning it in year 11 (after the ten years of (a)) is still the failure.
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 17(1)(b)
#TRACE `Art 17(1)(b) the Commissioner must not assign the registered number` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` AT (Day (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `assign the registered number of the entity to another registered charity` `the Commissioner` AT (Day (YMD 2037 6 1))
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 17(1)(b)
#TRACE `Art 17(1)(b) the Commissioner must not assign the registered number` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` AT (Day (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `assign the registered number of the entity to another registered charity` `the Commissioner` AT (Day (YMD 2027 1 1))
-- EXPECT: STANDING assign the registered number of the entity to another registered charity
#TRACE `Art 17(1)(b) the Commissioner must not assign the registered number` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` AT (Day (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` (Day (YMD 2080 1 1)))
-- F6.6, the discriminating case: a reassignment attempt in year 11. On the other reading the bar lasts the ten years of (a): assigning on 2 June 2036 is free, on 1 June 2036 it is not.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(1)(b) the Commissioner must not assign the registered number` (`the readings taken but with F6.6 read as` `the bar on assigning the registered number lasts for the ten years of Article 17(1)(a)`) `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` AT (Day (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `assign the registered number of the entity to another registered charity` `the Commissioner` AT (Day (YMD 2036 6 2))
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 17(1)(b)
#TRACE `Art 17(1)(b) the Commissioner must not assign the registered number` (`the readings taken but with F6.6 read as` `the bar on assigning the registered number lasts for the ten years of Article 17(1)(a)`) `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` AT (Day (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `assign the registered number of the entity to another registered charity` `the Commissioner` AT (Day (YMD 2036 6 1))

-- The bar as a fact about a day. Ten years from 1 June 2026: the last day is 1 June 2036.
#ASSERT       `Art 17(1)(b) the registered number may not be assigned on the day` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` (YMD 2037 6 1)
#ASSERT       `Art 17(1)(b) the registered number may not be assigned on the day` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(1)(b) the registered number may not be assigned on the day` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` (YMD 2026 5 31)
#ASSERT       `Art 17(1)(b) the registered number may not be assigned on the day` (`the readings taken but with F6.6 read as` `the bar on assigning the registered number lasts for the ten years of Article 17(1)(a)`) `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` (YMD 2036 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(1)(b) the registered number may not be assigned on the day` (`the readings taken but with F6.6 read as` `the bar on assigning the registered number lasts for the ten years of Article 17(1)(a)`) `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` (YMD 2036 6 2)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(1)(b) the registered number may not be assigned on the day` (`the readings taken but with F6.6 read as` `the bar on assigning the registered number lasts for the ten years of Article 17(1)(a)`) `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` (YMD 2037 6 1)
-- ... and on the other reading the bar starts on the day the ten years start (1 June 2026), not before.
#ASSERT       `Art 17(1)(b) the registered number may not be assigned on the day` (`the readings taken but with F6.6 read as` `the bar on assigning the registered number lasts for the ten years of Article 17(1)(a)`) `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(1)(b) the registered number may not be assigned on the day` (`the readings taken but with F6.6 read as` `the bar on assigning the registered number lasts for the ten years of Article 17(1)(a)`) `a retrospective deregistration by notice of 1 June 2026, effective from 1 June 2021` (YMD 2026 5 31)

§§ `Article 17(5) -- the remaining property`

-- Positional construction of a piece of property: what it is; the day acquired; whether it remains.
`a donation received on 31 December 2024 that remains` MEANS `Property of the charity` OF "a donation", (YMD 2024 12 31), TRUE
`a donation received on 1 January 2025 that remains` MEANS `Property of the charity` OF "a donation", (YMD 2025 1 1), TRUE
`a donation received on 1 June 2025, between the past date and the notice, that remains` MEANS `Property of the charity` OF "a donation", (YMD 2025 6 1), TRUE
`a donation received on 31 March 2026 that remains` MEANS `Property of the charity` OF "a donation", (YMD 2026 3 31), TRUE
`a donation received on 1 April 2026, the day of the notice, that remains` MEANS `Property of the charity` OF "a donation", (YMD 2026 4 1), TRUE
`a donation received on 31 December 2024 that has been spent` MEANS `Property of the charity` OF "a donation", (YMD 2024 12 31), FALSE

-- src:453 | (5) Paragraphs (6) to (11) apply, after a charity is deregistered, if and so long as there remains any property of the charity that was acquired before it was deregistered (the “remaining property”).
-- (5) Paragraphs (6) to (11) apply, after a charity is deregistered, if and so long as there remains any property of the charity that was acquired before it was deregistered. "Before" is strict.
-- Retrospective from 1 January 2025 by a notice of 1 April 2026. The reading taken: "deregistered" is 1 January 2025 for all purposes (paragraph (3)).
#ASSERT       `Art 17(5) the property is remaining property` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice` `a donation received on 31 December 2024 that remains`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(5) the property is remaining property` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice` `a donation received on 1 January 2025 that remains`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(5) the property is remaining property` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice` `a donation received on 1 June 2025, between the past date and the notice, that remains`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(5) the property is remaining property` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice` `a donation received on 31 December 2024 that has been spent`
-- F6.4, the discriminating case: a donation received between the past date and the notice. Not remaining property on the reading taken; remaining property if "deregistered" is the date of the notice.
#ASSERT       `Art 17(5) the property is remaining property` (`the readings taken but with F6.4 read as` `acquired before the date of the deregistration notice`) `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice` `a donation received on 1 June 2025, between the past date and the notice, that remains`
#ASSERT       `Art 17(5) the property is remaining property` (`the readings taken but with F6.4 read as` `acquired before the date of the deregistration notice`) `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice` `a donation received on 31 March 2026 that remains`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(5) the property is remaining property` (`the readings taken but with F6.4 read as` `acquired before the date of the deregistration notice`) `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice` `a donation received on 1 April 2026, the day of the notice, that remains`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(5) the property is remaining property` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice` `a donation received on 1 April 2026, the day of the notice, that remains`
-- Without retrospective effect the two readings coincide: the date of the notice is the date deregistered.
#ASSERT       `Art 17(5) the property is remaining property` `the readings taken` `a deregistration without retrospective effect` `a donation received on 31 March 2026 that remains`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(5) the property is remaining property` `the readings taken` `a deregistration without retrospective effect` `a donation received on 1 April 2026, the day of the notice, that remains`
#ASSERT       `Art 17(5) the property is remaining property` (`the readings taken but with F6.4 read as` `acquired before the date of the deregistration notice`) `a deregistration without retrospective effect` `a donation received on 31 March 2026 that remains`
-- Paragraphs (6) to (11) apply if some property acquired before the deregistration remains.
#ASSERT       `Art 17(5) paragraphs (6) to (11) apply` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice` (LIST `a donation received on 31 December 2024 that has been spent`, `a donation received on 31 December 2024 that remains`)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(5) paragraphs (6) to (11) apply` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice` (LIST `a donation received on 31 December 2024 that has been spent`, `a donation received on 1 June 2025, between the past date and the notice, that remains`)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(5) paragraphs (6) to (11) apply` `the readings taken` `a retrospective deregistration whose past date is specified in the deregistration notice` EMPTY

§§ `Article 17(6) and (7) -- the preserved purposes, and no power to amend them`

`the register entry of a deregistered charity` MEANS `Registered charity` WITH
    entity IS Entity WITH
        name IS "Hope Society"
        `standing on the register` IS `formerly registered and entered in the historic section`
        `kinds of entity` IS LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`
        `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
        governors IS EMPTY
        purposes IS EMPTY
    `registration number` IS "1"
    `registered name` IS "Hope Society"
    `alternative registered names` IS EMPTY
    `date registered` IS YMD 2019 1 1
    `date deregistered` IS JUST (YMD 2026 4 1)
    `registered charitable purposes` IS LIST "relief of poverty", "advancement of education"
    `registered public benefit statement` IS "a food bank and a school"
    `is an organized religious charity` IS FALSE

-- src:454 | (6) The entity must continue to apply the remaining property for the purposes that were its registered charitable purposes immediately before deregistration (the “preserved charitable purposes”), and in accordance with the registered public benefit statement that was in effect immediately before deregistration (the “preserved public benefit statement”).
-- (6) The entity must continue to apply the remaining property for the purposes that were its registered charitable purposes immediately before deregistration (the preserved charitable purposes), and in accordance with the
-- registered public benefit statement that was in effect then (the preserved public benefit statement).
#ASSERT       `Art 17(6) the preserved charitable purposes` `the register entry of a deregistered charity` EQUALS LIST "relief of poverty", "advancement of education"
#ASSERT       `Art 17(6) the preserved public benefit statement` `the register entry of a deregistered charity` EQUALS "a food bank and a school"
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(6) the entity must apply the remaining property for the preserved purposes` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the entity after its deregistration` DOES `apply the remaining property for the preserved charitable purposes and in accordance with the preserved public benefit statement` `the entity after its deregistration` AT 30
-- No period is stated: a standing duty for as long as property remains.
-- EXPECT: STANDING apply the remaining property for the preserved charitable purposes
#TRACE `Art 17(6) the entity must apply the remaining property for the preserved purposes` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)
-- Once no property remains the duty is over.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(6) the entity must apply the remaining property for the preserved purposes` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- src:455 | (7) Despite any provision of the entity’s constitution, or of the constitutional Law of the entity, the entity has no power to amend the preserved charitable purposes or preserved public benefit statement.
-- (7) Despite any provision of the entity's constitution, or of the constitutional Law of the entity, the entity has no power to amend the preserved charitable purposes or preserved public benefit statement.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(7) the entity has power to amend the preserved purposes or statement` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(7) the entity has power to amend the preserved purposes or statement` TRUE FALSE
-- Once paragraphs (6) to (11) no longer apply the Article says nothing, and the constitution decides.
#ASSERT       `Art 17(7) the entity has power to amend the preserved purposes or statement` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(7) the entity has power to amend the preserved purposes or statement` FALSE FALSE

§§ `Article 17(8) -- the entity may apply to the court to amend them`

-- src:456 | (8) The entity may apply to the court for an order amending the preserved charitable purposes or preserved public benefit statement, and the court may make such amending order, and any ancillary order, as it considers expedient to ensure that the remaining property continues to be applied for purposes that are, in the opinion of the court, charitable purposes and in a manner that, in the opinion of the court, provides public benefit.
-- (8) The entity may apply to the court for an order amending the preserved charitable purposes or preserved public benefit statement, and the court may make such amending order, and any ancillary order, as it considers expedient.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(8) the entity may apply to the court to amend the preserved purposes or statement` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the entity after its deregistration` DOES `apply to the court for an order amending the preserved charitable purposes or the preserved public benefit statement` `the entity after its deregistration` AT 8
-- EXPECT: STANDING apply to the court for an order amending the preserved charitable purposes
#TRACE `Art 17(8) the entity may apply to the court to amend the preserved purposes or statement` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(8) the entity may apply to the court to amend the preserved purposes or statement` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)
-- The court's power: both an amending order and any ancillary order, when the entity has applied and the court considers the order expedient to ensure the property is applied for charitable purposes and public benefit.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(8) the court may make an amending order and any ancillary order` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `make an amending order` `the court` AT 5
    PARTY `the court` DOES `make an order ancillary to an amending order` `the court` AT 6
-- EXPECT: STANDING make an order ancillary to an amending order
#TRACE `Art 17(8) the court may make an amending order and any ancillary order` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `make an amending order` `the court` AT 5
-- Without an application, without the court's view, or after no property remains: no such power.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(8) the court may make an amending order and any ancillary order` TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(8) the court may make an amending order and any ancillary order` TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(8) the court may make an amending order and any ancillary order` FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

§§ `Article 17(9) to (11) -- the court's powers over the deregistered entity`

-- src:457 | (9) The court may exercise any of the powers set out in Article 14 in relation to the deregistered entity, as if it were still registered, if, on an application by the Attorney General or a governor of the entity, it appears to the court –
-- src:458 | (a) that there is or has been any conduct in the administration of the entity in relation to the remaining property, that would have been misconduct if the entity had not been deregistered; or
-- src:459 | (b) that it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power for the purpose of protecting the remaining property or securing a proper application of the remaining property for the preserved charitable purposes of the entity and in accordance with the preserved public benefit statement.
-- (9) The court may exercise any of the powers set out in Article 14 in relation to the deregistered entity, as if it were still registered, if, on an application by the Attorney General or a governor of the entity,
-- it appears to the court (a) conduct that would have been misconduct, or (b) that it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power to protect or apply the remaining property.
-- Attorney General applies, conduct that would have been misconduct: the court may make an order of any of the kinds of Article 14(3).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(9) the court may exercise its Article 14 powers over the deregistered entity` TRUE `the Attorney General` TRUE FALSE `an order appointing a person to manage the affairs of the charity in place of its governors` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `exercise a power of Article 14 over the deregistered entity` `the court` `an order appointing a person to manage the affairs of the charity in place of its governors` AT 15
-- A governor applies, and it is necessary or desirable to protect the remaining property (limb (b) only).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(9) the court may exercise its Article 14 powers over the deregistered entity` TRUE `a governor` FALSE TRUE `an order suspending or removing a governor or another person concerned in the management` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `exercise a power of Article 14 over the deregistered entity` `the court` `an order suspending or removing a governor or another person concerned in the management` AT 15
-- A power not used stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING exercise a power of Article 14 over the deregistered entity
#TRACE `Art 17(9) the court may exercise its Article 14 powers over the deregistered entity` TRUE `the Attorney General` TRUE TRUE `an order making ancillary provision` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)
-- Each limb alone leaves the power standing (limb (a) only; limb (b) only).
-- EXPECT: STANDING exercise a power of Article 14 over the deregistered entity
#TRACE `Art 17(9) the court may exercise its Article 14 powers over the deregistered entity` TRUE `the Attorney General` TRUE FALSE `an order making ancillary provision` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)
-- EXPECT: STANDING exercise a power of Article 14 over the deregistered entity
#TRACE `Art 17(9) the court may exercise its Article 14 powers over the deregistered entity` TRUE `a governor` FALSE TRUE `an order making ancillary provision` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)
-- Neither limb: no power. An application by somebody else (the Commissioner): no power. No remaining property: no power.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(9) the court may exercise its Article 14 powers over the deregistered entity` TRUE `the Attorney General` FALSE FALSE `an order making ancillary provision` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(9) the court may exercise its Article 14 powers over the deregistered entity` TRUE `the Commissioner` TRUE TRUE `an order making ancillary provision` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(9) the court may exercise its Article 14 powers over the deregistered entity` FALSE `the Attorney General` TRUE TRUE `an order making ancillary provision` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- src:460 | (10) A governor may not apply under paragraph (9) unless the governor has first given notice to the Attorney General of the governor’s intention to do so and of the reasons for that intention.
-- (10) A governor may not apply under paragraph (9) unless the governor has first given notice to the Attorney General of the governor's intention to do so and of the reasons for that intention.
#ASSERT       `Art 17(10) the governor may apply under paragraph (9)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 17(10) the governor may apply under paragraph (9)` FALSE
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 17(10)
#TRACE `Art 17(10) a governor may not apply without first notifying the Attorney General` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `apply to the court under paragraph (9)` `a governor` AT 3
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(10) a governor may not apply without first notifying the Attorney General` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `apply to the court under paragraph (9)` `a governor` AT 3
-- EXPECT: STANDING apply to the court under paragraph (9)
#TRACE `Art 17(10) a governor may not apply without first notifying the Attorney General` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- src:461 | (11) The Attorney General may at any time, by giving notice to the governor and the court, take over an application made by a governor under paragraph (9), and may then withdraw or proceed with the application as the Attorney General sees fit.
-- (11) The Attorney General may at any time, by giving notice to the governor and the court, take over an application made by a governor under paragraph (9), and may then withdraw or proceed with the application.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(11) the Attorney General may take over the application of a governor` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Attorney General` DOES `take over the application of a governor` `the Attorney General` AT 5
    PARTY `the Attorney General` DOES `withdraw the application` `the Attorney General` AT 9
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(11) the Attorney General may take over the application of a governor` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Attorney General` DOES `take over the application of a governor` `the Attorney General` AT 5
    PARTY `the Attorney General` DOES `proceed with the application` `the Attorney General` AT 9
-- Taken over, nothing yet decided: the choice between withdrawing and proceeding stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING withdraw the application
#TRACE `Art 17(11) the Attorney General may take over the application of a governor` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Attorney General` DOES `take over the application of a governor` `the Attorney General` AT 5
-- No period is stated ("at any time"): the permission to take over stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING take over the application of a governor
#TRACE `Art 17(11) the Attorney General may take over the application of a governor` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)
-- No application by a governor: nothing to take over.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 17(11) the Attorney General may take over the application of a governor` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)
